petra 0

# Three 1 1/8 inch bolts. Table J3.3 lists holes for bolts to 1 inch and gives a formula for
# larger ones, which the rules do not read. So four lines are open: the clear spacing, the
# strength of the bolts and their holes, and the rupture and the block shear of each plate.
# By hand, with a hole of 1 1/8 + 1/8 inch, all four hold at 45 kip: the bolts carry
# 35.89 + 35.89 + 40.26 = 112.0 kip, and each plate ruptures at 145.4 and tears out at 145.6.
# The rules that read no hole are proved: 3 inch between centres, 1.5 inch to an end and to a
# side (Table J3.4), 12 inch at most between holes, and yielding at 129.6 kip.

plate tab {
  thickness 0.5 inch
  width 8 inch
  Fy given tab.Fy
  Fu given tab.Fu
}

plate strap {
  thickness 0.5 inch
  width 8 inch
  Fy given strap.Fy
  Fu given strap.Fu
}

lap splice {
  fastener "Group 120"
  threads included
  diameter 1.125 inch
  holes standard
  count 3
  pitch 3.5 inch
  end 2 inch
  side 4 inch
  surface protected
  joins tab strap
}
